+
+## 7. Duplicate files (`:core`)
+
+Package `com.pengstem.baidunetgo.core.dedup`. Mirrors the desktop Go engine
+(`internal/dedup`): it reads no file content, comparing only the size and unscrambled
+MD5 every listing already carries. Exact shipped API:
+
+```kotlin
+data class DedupKey(val size: Long, val md5: String)
+
+data class DedupFile(
+    val path: String,      // full netdisk path, e.g. "/文档/读我.txt"
+    val name: String, val size: Long, val fsId: Long,
+    val md5: String,       // unscrambled; "" when the netdisk gave none
+    val modified: Long,    // seconds, server_mtime
+)
+
+data class DedupGroup(val key: DedupKey, val files: List<DedupFile>) {
+    val size: Long get() = key.size                 // size of one copy
+    val total: Long get() = key.size * files.size   // size of every copy
+    val reclaim: Long get() = key.size * (files.size - 1)  // freed by keeping one
+}
+
+data class DedupProgress(val dir: String, val dirs: Int, val files: Int)
+data class DedupScanResult(
+    val files: List<DedupFile>, val dirs: Int,
+    val failed: List<String>, val truncated: Boolean,
+)
+data class DedupGrouping(val groups: List<DedupGroup>, val skipped: Int)
+
+object Dedup {
+    const val DefaultConcurrency = 4
+    const val DefaultMaxFiles = 50_000
+    const val DefaultMaxDirs = 5_000
+
+    suspend fun scan(netdisk: Netdisk, root: String = "/",
+                     concurrency: Int = DefaultConcurrency,
+                     maxFiles: Int = DefaultMaxFiles, maxDirs: Int = DefaultMaxDirs,
+                     onProgress: (DedupProgress) -> Unit = {}): DedupScanResult
+    fun group(files: List<DedupFile>): DedupGrouping
+    fun without(groups: List<DedupGroup>, gone: Set<String>): List<DedupGroup>
+}
+```
+
+`scan` walks `root` and every subfolder breadth-first, `concurrency` folders at a time,
+collecting each non-folder entry once (repeated fsIds deduped) and building full paths
+(`parent.trimEnd('/') + "/" + name`; a blank root means `/`). A folder that cannot be
+read is recorded in `failed` and skipped, unless it is the root, whose error is
+rethrown; it stops at `maxFiles`/`maxDirs` with `truncated = true`, reports
+`onProgress` after each folder, and aborts on `CancellationException`.
+
+`group` groups files by (size, md5): 0-byte/negative files are dropped, files with a
+blank md5 are counted in `skipped`, copies are deduped by non-zero fsId, and within a
+group they are sorted by modified ascending then path — `files[0]` is the copy to keep.
+Only groups of two or more are returned, ordered by `reclaim` desc, then size desc,
+then md5 asc. `without` removes the files at paths in `gone`, keeps each group's other
+copies as they were, drops groups that fall below two, and re-sorts the same way, so
+the results of a scan minus what it deleted are exactly what `group` would find left.
